1
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:09,500
It's my life, it's your life, fighting for
tomorrow, go catch what you really want.

2
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:13,317
I want more, anyone more,
come on, open up the door.

3
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:17,620
It's my life, it's your life, run
like a wind, jump high, yeah, yeah.

4
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:21,700
I know you're strong, believe
you can achieve your call.

5
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,360
Let's keep on going, I'll not stay.

6
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:45,617
Let's do it again.

7
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:47,457
You know what I mean, baby!

8
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:50,037
No one can make my dream come true?

9
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,260
Don't you feel it?

10
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:55,197
I really don't know what is
Something is testing me every day.

11
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,557
Hey, let's go.

12
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:57,477
Let's fly away.

13
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:00,577
I know I never wanna come back here.

14
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:01,797
Hey, let's go.

15
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:05,597
Let's fly away the great
end of the unknown rules.

16
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:07,437
Standing up, blowing up.

17
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,657
My dream is getting wilder.

18
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:12,617
I'm not afraid, beat me, hit me.

19
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,137
I will never turn around.

20
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:17,917
Another day, another chance.

21
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,097
You know it's never too late.

22
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:23,517
If I can do it, so can you only wait out.

23
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:26,017
We can let go together,
baby, crawling around.

24
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:28,477
It's my life, it's your life.

25
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:31,557
Party for tomorrow, go
get what you really want.

26
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:33,637
I want more, anyone more.

27
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:35,620
Come on, open up the door.

28
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,917
It's my life, it's your life.

29
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,957
Run like a wind, jump high, yeah, yeah.

30
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,597
I know you're strong.

31
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:45,037
Believe you can achieve your goal.

32
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,077
Let's keep on going, roaring.

33
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,337
It's my life, it's your life.

34
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:52,477
Fighting for your eyes that
I want, but your weary ones.

35
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:54,517
I want more, and you want more.

36
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:57,337
Come on, open up the gate.

37
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:59,757
It's my life, it's your light.

38
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,857
Shine like a star to be good, yeah.

39
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:03,617
I know you're strong.

40
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,257
Just that you can't achieve your best.

41
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:08,600
Let's keep on going out of day.

42
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:19,020
You make my day every day.

43
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,300
You're talking?

44
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,160
Since when can you speak?

45
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:41,720
Always could.

46
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:46,397
You mean...

47
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:49,068
you've lied to your
brother this whole time?

48
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:52,340
I never once indicated to
him that I became mute.

49
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:55,597
That is a crazy assumption
the guy made on his own.

50
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:56,797
You're being deceitful!

51
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:57,710
Why not correcting me?

52
00:02:57,793 --> 00:02:58,760
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

53
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:00,440
Silence now.

54
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:06,410
Huh?

55
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:16,520
Oh, the sound stopped. Where'd it go?

56
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:17,990
How?

57
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:22,437
It looks like people are talking,
but I can't hear anything.

58
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:25,344
You were being loud, so
I took a countermeasure.

59
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:26,940
They can't hear us.

60
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:30,302
Just like how you can't
hear a peep from outside.

61
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:33,000
I put up a soundproof wall to cover us.

62
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:37,340
I ate the calm calm fruit
and became a silent man.

63
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:42,680
You have Devil Fruit powers.

64
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,340
You're insane.

65
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:47,780
It's all for a lie.

66
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:49,310
Wait a sec.

67
00:03:49,393 --> 00:03:51,713
You faked the accidents too, didn't you?

68
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:53,880
That's right.

69
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:55,620
You're a sharp cookie.

70
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:57,897
The whole klutz thing is an act.

71
00:03:57,980 --> 00:04:00,039
You caught on fire again, you liar!

72
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:03,664
I've been clumsy my whole life.

73
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:04,879
That won't change.

74
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:06,277
There, you happy now?

75
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:07,301
Give me a break!

76
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:10,237
You mean to tell me that's
the only truth to you?

77
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:13,197
Why are you hiding all this
crap from your friends?

78
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,840
They're not my friends.

79
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:15,997
I'm with them.

80
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:18,240
But not by choice.

81
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:21,504
Someone's gotta curb my
brother Duffy's rampage.

82
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:24,057
It's hard to believe we're related.

83
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:27,081
Our parents showed us
nothing but love, after all.

84
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:34,780
But that monster has no humanity.

85
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:37,520
Help me!

86
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:42,280
Please, my boys are innocent!

87
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:45,700
Director, how is it made of them?

88
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,180
I beg you, please don't
harm my children anymore.

89
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:53,020
Help, Daddy.

90
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:54,580
It hurts everywhere.

91
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,240
I want to die.

92
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:58,400
I'll get even.

93
00:04:58,820 --> 00:05:00,100
I swear it.

94
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:02,520
Sophie, no.

95
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:03,780
You wretches!

96
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,300
I won't die today.

97
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:13,940
I swear to survive whatever
torment you throw at me!

98
00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:16,460
Remember my words!

99
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:22,540
I look forward to the day that I hunt you
down and murder every single one of you!

100
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,280
He's dangerous.

101
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:27,819
My brother's innately wicked
nature knows no bounds.

102
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,647
The only people who have seen
the full extent of his brutality

103
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:39,540
are the four executives, including
me and the first Corazon, Vergo.

104
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:41,300
Who's Vergo?

105
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:43,540
An extremely powerful individual.

106
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:47,197
Right now, he's away from the
family on a secret operation.

107
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:50,221
But the details of that
are between him and Duffy.

108
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:53,713
That guy has nothing to do
with you, so forget about him.

109
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:57,166
You can't turn into a
monster like my brother.

110
00:05:57,460 --> 00:06:00,700
Now scram, quickly. No
way! I'm not leaving!

111
00:06:00,940 --> 00:06:02,881
That's exactly what I want to be!

112
00:06:03,380 --> 00:06:06,037
Look, you possess the secret name of D.

113
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,617
You realize what that means?

114
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,406
You're part of a fateful few.

115
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:12,697
Growing up, when children
misbehaved, we were told,

116
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:16,220
if you don't fall in line,
you'll be eaten alive by D.

117
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:24,206
Every so often, another person with D in
their name would gain public attention.

118
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:27,594
You'd overhear the elderly
making passing comments like,

119
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:32,160
D will surely bring a new storm.

120
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:34,280
The hell's that mean?

121
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:36,940
You trying to say I'm a monster, then?

122
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:39,170
Perhaps.

123
00:06:39,253 --> 00:06:42,837
The details are still unknown, but
that name survived for centuries,

124
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:45,780
and has been muttered
across the entire world.

125
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,442
One more thing.

126
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:51,544
Those who fear the inheritors of
D have given them another title.

127
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:57,400
Sworn enemy of gods.

128
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:02,690
Gods?

129
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:05,800
If celestial dragons are
gods in this analogy,

130
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:10,460
the purpose of your people might
be the destruction of this world.

131
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:17,120
But look, this meaning of
destruction is different than Dofis.

132
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:21,380
It's a force that opposes
the order of heaven itself.

133
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:25,797
Why are you spouting this crap at me?!

134
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:28,360
I joined your dumb family for one purpose!

135
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,187
To kill people before I die!

136
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:32,197
Don't assume I want to work for you!

137
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:34,360
I only answer to Doflamingo!

138
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:36,217
What would I want to leave for?

139
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,418
I'm just gonna die in a year anyway!

140
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:41,880
There's gotta be a cure out
there somewhere. Shut up!

141
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:44,920
I'm so ready, you're out! Sucker!

142
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,017
Doflamingo will be angry!

143
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:47,930
Hey, wait!

144
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:51,297
Bet he freaks out when
he learns you can talk!

145
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:52,260
You damn brat!

146
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:00,300
I'm way stronger than two years ago.

147
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:01,380
Later, jerk!

148
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:05,740
You moron!

149
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:08,157
You broke the blood law a second time!

150
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:11,537
Hey, why were you moving your
mouths but not saying anything?

151
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:13,897
I'll buy you both ice cream
if you shut up about it.

152
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:14,810
Really?

153
00:08:14,893 --> 00:08:16,800
I'll take a 500-berry king-size cone.

154
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,668
Baby Five, can you spot me?

155
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:20,730
Huh? Okay.

156
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:22,440
Oh, my gosh.

157
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:24,740
He really needs me for something.

158
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:30,320
My time's up.

159
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:40,817
Damn it.

160
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,437
I shouldn't have trusted that kid.

161
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:43,940
I screwed up royally.

162
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,160
Corazon, we're about to set sail.

163
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:51,206
The Navy's on our tail again.

164
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:52,559
Zuru's on our way.

165
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:53,490
We gotta go.

166
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:56,500
Hasn't he said anything yet?

167
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:01,220
I decided not to tell.

168
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:03,740
I gave it some thought.

169
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:08,017
And remembered that I owed you for
keeping quiet back when I stabbed you.

170
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:09,571
I'd call that about even.

171
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:24,020
Anyone seen Ham or Law? What?

172
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:28,180
I swear I saw them board
together. They aren't here?

173
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:32,940
We need the extra firepower
and can't find either of them.

174
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:34,752
And I looked everywhere.

175
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:39,446
Young Master, found this
in Corazon's hammock.

176
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:43,220
Looks like they took off together.

177
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:45,326
What the hell is he thinking?

178
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:52,720
Un-tie me right now!

179
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:55,137
Hey, pick up that transponder still!

180
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,457
It's Joe Flamingo, isn't it?

181
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:57,997
I'll talk, just pick it up!

182
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,680
Come on, pick it up!

183
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:01,620
What's wrong with you?

184
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,360
Joe Flamingo, help!

185
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:06,060
What are you gonna do to me?

186
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:13,257
What are you calling up?

187
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:16,497
Hey, come and rescue me!

188
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:22,357
Rice crackers Cookies, it's me.

189
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:24,257
Oh brucinante.

190
00:10:24,340 --> 00:10:27,620
Hey, uh, need some time off?

191
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:38,237
You run into trouble—it's
a personal matter.

192
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,277
I see, understood?

193
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:41,257
How are the little ones doing?

194
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:43,557
Think you can scare them off soon?

195
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:46,157
I think those three are staying.

196
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,070
That

197
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:50,777
family is becoming infamous
now—take extra caution!

198
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:52,160
extra caution

199
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:57,960
Do as you see fit.

200
00:10:58,140 --> 00:11:00,611
I wholeheartedly entrust this case to you.

201
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,180
Just keep me updated.

202
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:03,970
Roger that.

203
00:11:04,053 --> 00:11:05,662
I'll send you a detailed report.

204
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:19,177
Admiral Sengoku!

205
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:22,025
The officer who asked
for reassignment is here.

206
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:23,460
Yes, yes, send him in.

207
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,160
You wanted to see me?

208
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:30,468
I've heard a lot about you.

209
00:11:31,140 --> 00:11:35,728
You've had quite a successful first year
and have been turning a lot of heads.

210
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:38,098
You wish to transfer to G5, correct?

211
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:40,111
What was your name again?

212
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:42,927
Also, FYI, there's half
an egg on your cheek.

213
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:45,080
Sir, name's Vergo.

214
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:49,832
Who'd you call just now?

215
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:51,520
Did you say report?

216
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:53,517
You've been hiding something?

217
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:55,117
Were you working with the Navy?

218
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,537
Got something against him?

219
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:59,077
The government and their allies sicken me!

220
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,572
Well, I ain't no Marine.

221
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:01,960
Is that a lie?

222
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:04,240
I won't go to the hospital!

223
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:07,897
You're acting like every
other brat in the world, Law.

224
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:10,300
I'll go to every hospital if I have to.

225
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:12,679
I'll find a cure for your sickness.

226
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,980
Look how big this one is.

227
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,729
I bet they can fix you up.

228
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,417
Get that kid out of here!

229
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,417
You can't catch white lead disease.

230
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,618
Isn't there any medicine for it yet?

231
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:27,160
M-m-might I ask?

232
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:28,516
Where were you born?

233
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:29,960
I'm from Flevance.

234
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,474
That's the White Town!

235
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:33,090
No!

236
00:12:33,173 --> 00:12:35,180
I don't want to get sick! Get it together!

237
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:37,717
We need anticeptic gloves and a gas mask!

238
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:41,220
Call security and notify
the government! Trotto!

239
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,580
No! No! Forget it!

240
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,270
Law!

241
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:46,190
See that?

242
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:47,960
I'm subhuman to them!

243
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:56,877
Please leave us alone, you white monster.

244
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,901
We don't want your gross disease.

245
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:03,397
How dare you bring that infected little
creature into a hospital of all places?

246
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:06,357
Do you realize you're putting
hundreds of patients at risk?

247
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:07,857
This is an emergency announcement.

248
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:11,411
A patient with white lead
disease is loose in the hospital.

249
00:13:15,540 --> 00:13:16,620
Get me back!

250
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:17,690
What a dangerous freak!

251
00:13:17,773 --> 00:13:20,640
All wards, prepare for sterilization.

252
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,240
Forget that hospital.

253
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:24,900
I'm real sorry.

254
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,937
Hope that didn't hit a
sore spot on you, kid.

255
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:28,960
I told you!

256
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:31,140
I didn't want to see a doctor!

257
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:34,420
Not all doctors suck like him.

258
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:37,677
I'm positive we'll find a good
one at this next hospital.

259
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,120
Don't force me to go!

260
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,440
He should be put down!

261
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:44,097
That's a severe case of
that white lead disease!

262
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:46,356
Take him away before he dooms us all!

263
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,060
Change of plans.

264
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,257
Let's try the next one.

265
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:51,170
Enough!

266
00:13:51,253 --> 00:13:52,260
I'm tired of this!

267
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,320
We've got an emergency! Help!

268
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:55,917
There's a flooded survivor!

269
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,457
You were supposed to purge them all!

270
00:13:57,540 --> 00:14:00,540
Look, all the people around
here seem kind-hearted!

271
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:01,610
No!

272
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:04,546
Take those filthy white
blotches away from us!

273
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:07,080
Screw you, buddy!

274
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:12,171
Eight hospitals have been hit as a boy
with white lead disease terrorizes...

275
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:13,940
I'm getting sicker.

276
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,475
I can't take anymore.

277
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:16,840
Shut up.

278
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:18,935
You'll find the cure.

279
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:20,275
You're not gonna die.

280
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:22,147
This next one will help you.

281
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:23,360
Don't give up.

282
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:25,400
White lead disease!

283
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,666
Put the hospital on lockdown!

284
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,480
I'm gonna kick your ass!

285
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:30,937
This kiddo needs your help!

286
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:32,040
I've had enough!

287
00:14:32,820 --> 00:14:33,650
Corazon!

288
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:53,480
What the hell am I doing?

289
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:57,557
I've been forcing this poor kid to relive

290
00:14:57,640 --> 00:15:00,960
his horrible childhood
over and over again.

291
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:03,619
He's not getting any better either.

292
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:07,226
I wondered if it was the
Will of D driving me.

293
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:10,020
No, I don't care about that anymore.

294
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:13,517
I just...

295
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:15,817
I just feel so sorry for this damn kid.

296
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:17,400
Knowing you.

297
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,717
You'd hate to hear this,

298
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:25,140
but this blubbering idiot is trying
everything he can to save you.

299
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,720
You're still a pain in the ass kid,

300
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:33,039
but hearing you talk about death—my

301
00:15:34,780 --> 00:15:36,877
heart can't take it.

302
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:40,637
You may have stabbed me,
you little shit! But?

303
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:41,550
but

304
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,020
It didn't hurt at all.

305
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:50,396
You were the one who was
actually suffering back then.

306
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:54,600
I just wanted to fix things for you, Mom.

307
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:13,810
Cora!

308
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:15,660
Hey, Cora!

309
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:17,940
Breakfast is done!

310
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,060
What's that face for?

311
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:22,690
What's that face for?

312
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:23,618
You called me Cora?

313
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:25,160
You said that, yeah?

314
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:26,891
You want the food or not?

315
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:30,780
Cora's own. It's me.

316
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:36,060
What's wrong?

317
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:38,560
I know you're there.

318
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:46,809
It's already been six months
since you took off on your own.

319
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:49,020
Is law still with you?

320
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,310
Doflamingo.

321
00:17:00,740 --> 00:17:01,740
I see.

322
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,692
Well, I'm glad both of you are all right.

323
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,646
Have you found a good doctor?

324
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:10,660
I had a feeling.

325
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:14,288
I think it's time you
come back to the ship.

326
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:17,260
We might be able to cure Law's disease.

327
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:23,800
I happen to find a lead
on the op-op fruit.

328
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:29,057
Some stupid pirates who don't know
what it's worth got their hands on it.

329
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:30,697
Seems the Navy caught wind,

330
00:17:30,780 --> 00:17:34,477
because now they're offering them a ton
of money and getting ready for trade.

331
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:38,501
As usual, the world government is
pulling strings to get their way.

332
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:40,940
It's risky, but we can steal it.

333
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:44,840
Once we have it,

334
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:47,280
due to the nature of its power,

335
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:51,880
I can only allow someone whose
loyalty I trust completely to eat it.

336
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:56,860
And that would be you, Corazon.

337
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,900
Afterwards, you can cure Law's disease.

338
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:09,457
What do you think?

339
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,300
I value your opinion.

340
00:18:11,700 --> 00:18:15,700
The Navy has been hounding us
everywhere we went quite consistently.

341
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:19,186
Saru, in particular,
always seemed to find us.

342
00:18:19,340 --> 00:18:21,060
But in the past six months,

343
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:24,593
the Navy hasn't reared its
ugly head around us even once.

344
00:18:24,820 --> 00:18:28,800
You'll note, that's exactly
how long Corazon's been gone.

345
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:33,805
You think your dear little brother has
been tipping off the Navy this whole time?

346
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,600
Could be a coincidence, though.

347
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:38,901
That's certainly what I'm hoping.

348
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:41,657
I don't want to distrust him, honestly.

349
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:44,980
We're still family after all.

350
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:49,337
Look at your law.

351
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:53,677
Forget those stupid
doctors—you're gonna make

352
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:56,017
it without them once
we get the op op fruit.

353
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:58,317
Your white lead disease
will be a thing of the past.

354
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:01,597
What's the op op fruit? Do it.

355
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,117
Lets you modify someone's body.

356
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:06,757
You can perform miracle operations
and cure any nasty diseases.

357
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:07,670
diseases

358
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:09,180
Yeah, right.

359
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,157
I don't believe in fairy tales.

360
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:12,070
It's real.

361
00:19:12,153 --> 00:19:13,196
But there's a catch.

362
00:19:13,580 --> 00:19:15,380
You need knowledge to use it.

363
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:19,080
But that's no problem.

364
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:21,877
Because I know you're the
son of a brilliant doctor.

365
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:24,317
One who was trusted by
the people of Flevins.

366
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:26,106
But why does that matter now?

367
00:19:26,820 --> 00:19:27,650
Are you kidding?

368
00:19:27,733 --> 00:19:30,417
It matters because you're
going to eat the fruit.

369
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,330
I am?

370
00:19:31,413 --> 00:19:34,574
Don't Flamingo said you were
supposed to eat it, though.

371
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:40,026
A person will die if he
eats two devil fruits.

372
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:45,827
Duffy only said that because he doesn't
know about my calm, calm fruit-ability.

373
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:48,800
We're through with Duffy.

374
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:51,400
We aren't going back to the family.

375
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:03,421
That decision became clear to me
as my journey with you dragged on.

376
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:08,920
By now, I'm sure Duffy has
realized that I'm a traitor

377
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:11,540
Uh, are you sure?

378
00:20:11,740 --> 00:20:15,117
On this snail, he said you
should eat the fruit, right?

379
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,537
There is a secondary reason
behind that decision.

380
00:20:17,620 --> 00:20:19,977
It has nothing to do with trust.

381
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:25,077
I get it, Duffy!

382
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:28,537
You want me to sacrifice myself
to give you eternal life!

383
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:30,317
And if I don't, I'm a traitor!

384
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:32,300
But either way, I'm dead.

385
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:36,060
Listen, we'll get the jump on Dofi.

386
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:39,949
We'll steal the Op-Op fruit
before anybody else can have it.

387
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:43,277
You'll eat the fruit
and cure your illness.

388
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:46,948
When you're better, we can go
into hiding somewhere together.

389
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,340
Prepare to set sail.

390
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:54,286
We'll get that fruit,
no matter what it takes.

391
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:58,790
Garlic.

392
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,540
Rice crackers!

393
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:02,820
Cookies. It's me.

394
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:05,057
Rosanante, it's been a while.

395
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:06,777
I've been worried about you.

396
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:10,420
Hey, Garp, could you step
out for a second? What? Why?

397
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:12,477
I just brought you snacks, didn't I?

398
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:14,137
At least offer me some tea.

399
00:21:14,220 --> 00:21:15,400
Bye, Admiral Garp.

400
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:17,900
Is now a bad time to chat, Sengoku?

401
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:19,817
Make your own damn tea.

402
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:20,897
I got work to do.

403
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:22,597
Now get out of here, you fool.

404
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,510
Shoo, shoo.

405
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:25,670
Yeah,

406
00:21:25,753 --> 00:21:30,264
well, I'm taking the rest of the snacks
with me if that's how you're going to act.

407
00:21:30,820 --> 00:21:31,897
Um, can I talk now?

408
00:21:31,980 --> 00:21:33,840
Yeah, sorry. Go ahead.

409
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:37,988
I heard you were looking to make
a trade for the op-op fruit.

410
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:42,280
Yes, but how did you know that?

411
00:21:42,780 --> 00:21:44,956
My brother caught wind of it somehow.

412
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,310
What?

413
00:21:47,393 --> 00:21:48,380
That's top secret info.

414
00:21:49,440 --> 00:21:50,340
I see.

415
00:21:50,620 --> 00:21:52,796
So that's who you're talking to, huh?

416
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:55,857
Where can I find the pirates
you're making the trade with?

417
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:56,770
I don't know.

418
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:59,797
If they're smart, they're
laying low right now.

419
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:02,317
And what if I told you that Doflamingo was

420
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:05,097
going to steal the fruit
before you could buy it?

421
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:06,010
Is he?

422
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:07,710
Weird.

423
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:11,160
I'm dizzy all of a sudden.

424
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:14,453
When and where are you making the trade?

425
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:17,782
Three weeks from now at
Rubeck in the North Blue.

426
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:20,710
Rubeck.

427
00:22:21,040 --> 00:22:23,797
I'll meet Dofie and his
friends on Swallow Island.

428
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:27,351
They should be there three days
before the handoff happens.

429
00:22:27,500 --> 00:22:29,097
That's where you'll be waiting?

430
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:31,597
I imagine he won't want
to take any chances,

431
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:34,417
so he'll likely bring the
entire family with him.

432
00:22:34,500 --> 00:22:35,735
Thanks for the intel.

433
00:22:36,440 --> 00:22:38,757
So we'll plan an ambush at Swallow Island.

434
00:22:38,840 --> 00:22:40,820
That'll be the end of Doflamingo.

435
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:45,157
It's a chance to catch the whole Don
Quixote family in one fell swoop.

436
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:47,420
Just make sure you stay away.

437
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:49,579
That was the plan.

438
00:22:50,340 --> 00:22:52,397
I've got a list I'll
be sending your way as

439
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:55,080
soon as I can of Dofie's
business partners.

440
00:22:55,780 --> 00:22:57,898
Big shots working behind the scenes.

441
00:22:59,180 --> 00:23:02,917
Bunch of dark little secrets
hiding there in the north.

442
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,757
Blue, I see, thank you.

443
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:06,980
Gotta lick!

444
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:09,230
Hey, law!

445
00:23:09,313 --> 00:23:10,877
You ready to take off?

446
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:11,997
Gotta move.

447
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:15,737
Are you okay?

448
00:23:15,820 --> 00:23:16,877
Come on, kid.

449
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:18,220
Stay with me!

450
00:23:19,780 --> 00:23:20,610
Not now.

451
00:23:20,693 --> 00:23:24,957
When we finally have a real chance to
save you, it hasn't been three years yet?

452
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:26,857
You said you had more time than this.

453
00:23:26,940 --> 00:23:28,237
You gotta hang in there.

454
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:29,849
Oh, jeez, the fever's bad.

455
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:31,797
What should I do?

456
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:32,957
Doctors are useless.

457
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:34,357
It's all up to me now to save him.

458
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:36,017
What am I supposed to do, Law?

459
00:23:36,100 --> 00:23:37,453
Give me a hint, please!

460
00:23:38,460 --> 00:23:40,460
You gotta pull through this, okay?

461
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:43,860
Just stay alive for three more weeks.

462
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:47,100
Give me a chance to make this right!

463
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:54,490
Damn it!

464
00:23:54,573 --> 00:23:56,202
Why did a storm have to hit now?

465
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:57,910
Couran.

466
00:23:58,220 --> 00:23:59,050
Huh?

467
00:23:59,133 --> 00:23:59,963
What's wrong, Ra?

468
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:04,880
All those years, the government
knew that my people would die.

469
00:24:05,080 --> 00:24:08,609
but they kept making us take
up that white land to get rich.

470
00:24:09,420 --> 00:24:13,080
The people of Lovitz and my family,

471
00:24:14,240 --> 00:24:15,320
the government?

472
00:24:15,980 --> 00:24:16,960
killed them.

473
00:24:20,320 --> 00:24:21,617
Tell me the truth.

474
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:24,277
Are you one of them working with the navy?

475
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:26,837
Are you a marine like the others?

476
00:24:26,920 --> 00:24:28,097
You're kidding me?

477
00:24:28,180 --> 00:24:30,280
No, I could never be a marine.

478
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:34,257
What a relief!

479
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:37,697
I'm with you, law, but listen to me, okay.

480
00:24:37,780 --> 00:24:40,460
Once you and I run away
with the up up fruit,

481
00:24:41,140 --> 00:24:44,437
we'll make enemies of everyone—doflamingo
the navy and the world

482
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:48,097
government—and they'll chase us to
the end of the world if they have to,

483
00:24:48,180 --> 00:24:52,077
so if you want to live, be
prepared to fight for it.

484
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:52,990
Any update

485
00:24:59,860 --> 00:25:01,477
on the location of those pirates, sengoku?

486
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:04,737
Yeah, they're hiding in a ghost town.

487
00:25:04,820 --> 00:25:06,717
In this place called
minion island—it's right to

488
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:09,537
the east of rubeck—where
they're making the trade.

489
00:25:09,620 --> 00:25:11,032
they're making the trade

490
00:25:11,180 --> 00:25:13,651
Seems like they have a hideout over there.

491
00:25:14,400 --> 00:25:16,860
The pirate's name is Diaz Barrels.

492
00:25:17,460 --> 00:25:18,500
That ring a bell?

493
00:25:19,160 --> 00:25:21,560
Yeah, he's a former Navy officer, right?

494
00:25:22,080 --> 00:25:22,910
Good memory.

495
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:27,464
Anyway, our lookout ship is
monitoring Minion Island as we speak.

496
00:25:28,820 --> 00:25:31,055
Everything he said seems to check out.

497
00:25:31,900 --> 00:25:34,757
We have everything set up
at Swallow Island, too.

498
00:25:34,840 --> 00:25:37,317
Near where you told Doflamingo
you were gonna meet him.

499
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:39,317
We brought two warships to deal with him.

500
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:41,400
We're ready for an Alto battle.

501
00:25:41,860 --> 00:25:45,177
I won't let Doe Flamingo get his
grubby fingers on the op-op fruit,

502
00:25:45,260 --> 00:25:46,672
no matter what it takes.

503
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:48,470
Okay.

504
00:25:48,553 --> 00:25:49,529
It won't be long now, Law.

505
00:25:49,960 --> 00:25:50,790
Wait here.

506
00:26:10,260 --> 00:26:11,090
Mr.

507
00:26:11,173 --> 00:26:12,380
EA, where's my booze?

508
00:26:12,480 --> 00:26:13,421
I need a refill!

509
00:26:14,320 --> 00:26:15,150
Right away.

510
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:17,740
All this money for one fruit!

511
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:20,374
You know how much they offered us, huh?

512
00:26:20,740 --> 00:26:22,420
Five billion berries, man!

513
00:26:24,620 --> 00:26:26,280
What a bunch of suckers!

514
00:26:26,540 --> 00:26:28,717
Is the government full of morons or what?

515
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:31,877
If we get that much money, we don't
even need to be pirates anymore!

516
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:34,195
We can just stuff our faces and party!

517
00:26:36,480 --> 00:26:38,197
Yeah, that sounds good to me!

518
00:26:38,280 --> 00:26:41,140
From what I understand about this thing,

519
00:26:41,480 --> 00:26:43,600
if a doctor gobbles it up,

520
00:26:43,860 --> 00:26:48,036
then he'll get the skills to be a
world-famous surgeon like none other.

521
00:26:49,800 --> 00:26:53,520
There was some legendary doctor
who ate it some time ago.

522
00:26:53,740 --> 00:26:56,617
They say he could perform
miracles with a scalpel,

523
00:26:56,700 --> 00:26:59,400
cure incurable diseases,
that sort of thing.

524
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:01,300
But what the hell do I care?

525
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:03,506
I don't need to be a surgeon.

526
00:27:03,780 --> 00:27:05,917
Not when you're as rich as we're gonna be.

527
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:06,830
Damn straight!

528
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:16,497
check this out law everything that's near

529
00:27:16,580 --> 00:27:20,560
me won't make a peep after i do this calm

530
00:27:29,560 --> 00:27:30,600
The face.

531
00:27:38,380 --> 00:27:39,840
Ugh, that stinks!

532
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:41,460
Just like magic!

533
00:27:41,720 --> 00:27:43,017
You didn't hear a thing, did you?

534
00:27:43,100 --> 00:27:43,930
Who cares?

535
00:27:44,080 --> 00:27:46,198
What the hell is that even good for?

536
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:48,380
It's totally dumb!

537
00:27:49,260 --> 00:27:51,760
BB-5's arms-arms power is way cool!

538
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:53,798
Yeah, you're right!

539
00:27:53,900 --> 00:27:56,371
I totally wish I could do that stuff, too!

540
00:27:56,940 --> 00:28:00,617
But when it comes to having a peaceful
night's sleep, no one beats me!

541
00:28:00,700 --> 00:28:01,530
What?

542
00:28:20,280 --> 00:28:22,100
What happened? An earthquake?

543
00:28:23,320 --> 00:28:24,150
Captain!

544
00:28:24,233 --> 00:28:27,117
I didn't hear an explosion,
but something blew up!

545
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:29,500
The coal pole's on fire! What?

546
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:31,565
Was there an explosion or not?

547
00:28:33,100 --> 00:28:34,020
My treasure!

548
00:28:34,260 --> 00:28:35,554
My treasure's running!

549
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:37,700
Put out the fire already!

550
00:28:38,080 --> 00:28:39,440
What's going on here?

551
00:28:42,060 --> 00:28:44,560
We must be under attack somehow, huh?

552
00:28:45,540 --> 00:28:47,037
The lights just went out.

553
00:28:47,120 --> 00:28:50,020
Where's all this glass
coming from? The lamps!

554
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:51,572
They were all shattered!

555
00:28:52,520 --> 00:28:54,638
Somebody, light a candle, would you?

556
00:28:56,780 --> 00:28:57,610
Come on!

557
00:28:57,693 --> 00:28:59,386
Doesn't anybody have a light?

558
00:29:26,420 --> 00:29:27,560
I got it, Law.

559
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:29,391
Just like I said I would.

560
00:29:29,940 --> 00:29:32,940
We're going to cure that
disease of yours right up.

561
00:29:43,180 --> 00:29:44,397
That freaked me out.

562
00:29:44,480 --> 00:29:45,310
Who's that?

563
00:29:45,393 --> 00:29:46,553
He fell out of nowhere.

564
00:29:47,980 --> 00:29:48,810
Hey!

565
00:29:48,893 --> 00:29:52,417
The guy in a black coat just stole the
all-bought fruit and he was coming this way!

566
00:29:52,500 --> 00:29:53,735
Don't let him escape!

567
00:29:56,120 --> 00:29:56,960
It's him!

568
00:30:11,780 --> 00:30:13,368
I know you've got it, Ruff.

569
00:30:13,660 --> 00:30:15,248
But wait for me here, okay?

570
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:23,860
I'll be back, and I'll have
the Arpuffroot with me too.
